Found during k252 (2026-10-31, ocp-status-worker). Not yet verified by the main agent: confirm before fixing. The text form of `ocp status` reports a failed cluster connect or a failed decrypt on STDOUT. That breaks the STDOUT/STDERR rule in .claude/rules/ocp-rules.md, which was written up in k105 and has k84 as precedent.

Done when the errors and their diagnosis go to STDERR, the report stays on STDOUT, and the exit code matches the outcome. A test pins each channel. Lane: ocp-status-worker.

2026-10-31 01:51 Verified (ocp-status-worker): reproduced in new t/257-status-text-stderr.t, run in Docker. Exit codes are already right (1 for decrypt and connect failure). The channels are wrong: Status.pm execute prints 'ERROR: Cannot decrypt kubeconfig.yaml' + 'Make sure .ocp/age.key exists.' and 'WARNING: Cannot connect to cluster API' + 'Error: …' on STDOUT, and STDERR stays empty. 4/15 red (tests 4-5, 10-11). The --json form already gets this right (t/230).

2026-10-31 01:56 Decision (mine, not the maintainer's): the 'Kubeconfig available. Export with: ocp kubeconfig -e' line after a failed connect stays on STDOUT. It is the report's kubeconfig hint, the same one a good run ends on, and not a diagnosis of the failure. Also chomp the API error, so STDERR does not get a blank line after 'Error: …'.
Also found (out of scope, not fixed): in both the text and the JSON form, the drift eval in execute/_collect_json is 'eval { OCP::Drift->new(...)->detect } // []', so if OCP::Drift itself dies, ocp status shows no drift and says nothing on STDERR. The kind=>'error' entries cover API failures inside detect, but not a die out of new/detect. Candidate card for the status lane.

2026-10-31 01:56 Done: lib/OCP/Cmd/Status.pm execute(). The decrypt failure (ERROR + age.key hint) and the connect failure (WARNING + 'Error: <cause>', now chomped) print to STDERR. The report on STDOUT is unchanged and the exit code stays 1. POD =description names the channels. New t/257-status-text-stderr.t pins each channel exactly (decrypt, API down, clean run with empty STDERR) plus the exit codes. Verified: DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 make test TESTS='t/257-status-text-stderr.t t/11-status-command.t t/230-status-json.t t/252-status-amd-gpu.t' → 4 files, 91 tests, PASS. Before the fix t/257 was 4/15 red. Mutation check 8/8 killed (each STDERR print reverted to STDOUT, chomp dropped, hint moved to STDERR, both return 1→0).

